From 135c7b478e06c9faabad8c275451be13a612f496 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Franke <afranke@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:16:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Size wow64 control messages by their data length.

wow64_translate_control() checked for room in the 32-bit control buffer
using the whole 64-bit cmsg_len, which already includes the 16-byte
64-bit header, as if it were the payload length. Each message therefore
asked for 16 more bytes than WSA_CMSG_SPACE() gives it, and a 32-bit
caller whose buffer is sized exactly got Control.len 0, MSG_CTRUNC and
WSAEMSGSIZE. With only IP_PKTINFO enabled, which needs 20 bytes, any
buffer under 36 bytes failed. The memcpy() also copied cmsg_len bytes
of payload instead of the payload length, reading past the 64-bit
message and writing into the reserved slack.

Use the payload length for the space check, the 32-bit cmsg_len and the
copy.

This matters more now that macOS delivers the TOS and TTL control
messages: a 32-bit application that sizes its buffer for IP_PKTINFO and
IP_TOS (36 bytes) would otherwise fail every receive instead of
receiving both.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/socket.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/socket.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/socket.c
index 71b30a5..40244ae 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/socket.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/socket.c
@@ -556,17 +556,18 @@ static int wow64_translate_control( const WSABUF *control64, struct afd_wsabuf_3
     {
         struct cmsghdr_32 *cmsg32 = (struct cmsghdr_32 *)ptr32;
         const WSACMSGHDR *cmsg64 = (const WSACMSGHDR *)ptr64;
+        const size_t data_len = cmsg64->cmsg_len - sizeof(*cmsg64);
 
-        if (ptr32 + sizeof(*cmsg32) + cmsg_align_32( cmsg64->cmsg_len ) > buf32 + max_len)
+        if (ptr32 + sizeof(*cmsg32) + cmsg_align_32( data_len ) > buf32 + max_len)
         {
             control32->len = 0;
             return 0;
         }
 
-        cmsg32->cmsg_len = cmsg64->cmsg_len - sizeof(*cmsg64) + sizeof(*cmsg32);
+        cmsg32->cmsg_len = sizeof(*cmsg32) + data_len;
         cmsg32->cmsg_level = cmsg64->cmsg_level;
         cmsg32->cmsg_type = cmsg64->cmsg_type;
-        memcpy( cmsg32 + 1, cmsg64 + 1, cmsg64->cmsg_len );
+        memcpy( cmsg32 + 1, cmsg64 + 1, data_len );
 
         ptr64 += WSA_CMSG_ALIGN( cmsg64->cmsg_len );
         ptr32 += cmsg_align_32( cmsg32->cmsg_len );
